{{#hasRedundantReads}}
## Redundant file reads

Files read more than once in the same session.

| Session | File | Reads | Span (min) | Max gap (min) | Pattern |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
{{#redundantReads}}
| `{{sessionId}}` | `{{filePath}}` | {{reads}} | {{spanMinutes}} | {{maxGapMinutes}} | {{pattern}} |
{{/redundantReads}}

`Pattern` distinguishes a tight **hunting loop** (≥ 3 reads, max gap ≤ 5 min — the agent is retrying or re-verifying) from **spread across session** (max gap ≥ 30 min — re-reads after long gaps, usually legitimate context refresh) and a **tight cluster** in between. Only hunting loops warrant a rule. Caveat: multi-agent workflows show up here too — five subagents each reading the same diff once looks like five reads in one session and is working as intended; check whether the session fanned out before writing a rule.

{{/hasRedundantReads}}
