Latency tails (p95) surface tools that occasionally do heavy work — long shell commands, slow MCP servers, large file reads. If a tool's p95 is much higher than its average, consider whether the agent could narrow its inputs (smaller globs, shorter shell pipelines, paged reads). `Agent` is the exception: subagents legitimately run for many minutes and return a short summary — high latency here is delegation working, not a defect.

